WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.000
Alright guys, so in this video, we are going to learn about premium and discount zones.

00:08.000 --> 00:11.080
What is a premium and a discount zone?

00:11.080 --> 00:19.480
So I am going to give you an example, let's say that you want to buy a house, right?

00:19.480 --> 00:24.160
And the prices are very high, okay?

00:24.160 --> 00:30.360
But you know that the prices are going to be lower in the future.

00:30.360 --> 00:36.300
So are you going to buy the house at a very high price or you're going to wait for price

00:36.300 --> 00:41.000
to lower down and then you buy?

00:41.000 --> 00:47.080
Of course, you're going to wait for price to lower so that you can buy it at a discount,

00:47.080 --> 00:48.960
if that makes sense.

00:48.960 --> 00:58.400
Similarly, whenever we want to go long, alright, we should always be buying at a discounted

00:58.400 --> 01:00.400
zone.

01:00.400 --> 01:05.840
Now how do we find a discounted or a premium zone?

01:05.840 --> 01:10.160
Now let me give you an example for premium zone, alright?

01:10.160 --> 01:18.480
So let's say that you bought a house at a very low price.

01:18.480 --> 01:25.040
Now you want to sell it, of course you are going to sell it for a higher price, okay?

01:25.040 --> 01:29.680
You don't want to sell it at a lower price because that's going to, you know, it won't

01:29.680 --> 01:31.280
be profitable for you.

01:31.280 --> 01:36.440
So that's why when you are going to sell your house, you are going to sell it at a higher

01:36.440 --> 01:37.440
price.

01:37.440 --> 01:42.720
Similarly, when you are about to short, when you're about to take a short position, you

01:42.720 --> 01:48.400
should be waiting for the price to come up at a premium level so that you can sell it

01:48.400 --> 01:50.360
if that makes sense, alright?

01:50.360 --> 01:55.040
You want the price to be higher in order for you to be selling it.

01:55.040 --> 02:00.400
So first of all, let me give you an example for a discounted zone, alright?

02:00.400 --> 02:04.240
So as you can see, price went up right up to this level, alright?

02:04.240 --> 02:13.240
So you can see price made a very huge move from this point to this point, alright?

02:13.240 --> 02:16.040
From this to this.

02:16.040 --> 02:19.600
Now, are you going to buy here?

02:19.600 --> 02:21.200
Absolutely not.

02:21.200 --> 02:26.000
If you are a trader, you should know that you should never be buying at around this

02:26.000 --> 02:28.000
level, okay?

02:28.000 --> 02:30.760
You should always be buying at a pullback, okay?

02:30.760 --> 02:36.880
So how do we determine a discounted zone?

02:36.880 --> 02:41.800
Well, what you want to do is you want to pull out your Fibonacci tool, alright?

02:41.800 --> 02:45.480
You go to the settings here, choose Fib retracement.

02:45.480 --> 02:55.120
You want to start from the very low of that push to the very top of that push, alright?

02:55.120 --> 03:02.560
And then you want to, first of all, you want to copy these settings, alright?

03:02.560 --> 03:09.520
You can pause the video right here and you want to copy these settings.

03:09.520 --> 03:18.080
Now when the price is below the 50% level, then the price is considered to be in a discounted

03:18.080 --> 03:19.440
area.

03:19.440 --> 03:28.080
I will repeat when the price, as you can see, when the price is below the 50% Fibonacci

03:28.080 --> 03:34.720
area, then the price is considered to be in a discounted zone.

03:34.720 --> 03:39.200
That is where you should be buying, alright?

03:39.200 --> 03:45.560
Now I will not tell you how to exactly enter in this video, but this is what I am telling

03:45.560 --> 03:46.560
you, alright?

03:46.560 --> 03:51.960
Just for the sake of this video that you should always be buying when the price falls

03:51.960 --> 03:55.240
into the discounted zone, alright?

03:55.240 --> 04:01.320
So as you can see, price pushed up from this point to this point, you should not be buying

04:01.320 --> 04:03.800
here or here or here, right?

04:03.800 --> 04:08.320
You should be waiting for price to fall down into the discounted zone, which is below the

04:08.320 --> 04:16.760
50% as you can see, and then this is the best area to be buying, okay?

04:16.760 --> 04:20.760
Let's talk about premium zones.

04:20.760 --> 04:30.040
So as you can see, we made a move from this level to this level, alright, we dropped down

04:30.040 --> 04:33.440
heavily from this point to this point.

04:33.440 --> 04:39.960
So similarly, we are going to draw our Fibonacci retracement tool from the very high of that

04:39.960 --> 04:48.640
move, from the start of that move, sorry, to the end of that move, which ends here, okay?

04:48.640 --> 04:52.720
Now you don't want to sell here, you don't want to sell here, you don't want to sell

04:52.720 --> 04:54.160
here.

04:54.160 --> 04:57.880
You should be waiting for price to come back into the premium zone.

04:57.880 --> 04:59.520
Now what is premium zone?

04:59.520 --> 05:08.440
Whenever price falls or goes, sorry, not falls, but whenever price goes into the premium zone,

05:08.440 --> 05:15.440
which is above 50%, alright, so whenever price goes above the 50%, then that price is considered

05:15.440 --> 05:18.400
to be in a premium zone.

05:18.400 --> 05:20.600
Now what does that mean?

05:20.600 --> 05:26.720
It means that this is a great area for you to be selling, okay?

05:26.720 --> 05:33.120
Now you don't want to just blindly sell off when price falls into the, you know, falls

05:33.120 --> 05:39.720
above the 50% or below the 50%, there are certain criteria that we should be discussing

05:39.720 --> 05:44.240
in the upcoming videos, but for now, all you want to know is what are discounted and premium

05:44.240 --> 05:45.680
zones, alright?

05:45.680 --> 05:52.920
So for price to be considered in a premium area, you should be waiting for the price

05:52.920 --> 05:59.200
to go above the 50% level of the Fibonacci, alright?

05:59.200 --> 06:03.000
So now this area is the best HV selling.

06:03.000 --> 06:10.600
So if you sold here, alright, you could have made a great profit, like this could be one

06:10.600 --> 06:15.680
to two risk reward, but of course, this is hindsight, but this is what I'm telling you,

06:15.680 --> 06:16.680
alright?

06:16.680 --> 06:22.160
You should always be selling at the premium zone and you should always be buying at a

06:22.160 --> 06:24.040
discounted zone.

06:24.040 --> 06:31.240
So I really hope that this video is clear and I really hope that you know what is premium

06:31.240 --> 06:33.240
and discounted zones.

06:33.240 --> 06:41.200
